fcitx5-nextless (10.12.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Capture-path behaviour fix (issue #61): with denoise=deepfilter, both legs
    of the 16k -> 48k -> 16k resample are now drained (soxr returns its
    group-delay tail only when end-of-input is signalled with in == NULL, not
    with ilen == 0), and deep-filter's own constant 30 ms is appended back from
    the raw input. A denoised utterance therefore keeps its full length instead
    of silently losing 69-97 ms off the end, which is where the last syllable
    lives. A response more than 160 ms short is treated as a malfunction and
    falls back to speexdsp rather than being padded into a half-denoised buffer.
  * Benchmark harness: bench_asr --denoise (and BACKENDS="deepfilter" in
    run_bench.sh) measures the add-on's own dfDenoise(). docs/benchmarks.md
    carries the first real-binary DeepFilterNet row - RTF 0.13-0.16, ~1.0-1.3 s
    per 5-10 s utterance, 60 MB - with the machine header and raw JSONL
    committed next to it.
  * README: the measured DeepFilterNet cost, and a new "Rolling back" section
    (apt remove vs purge, downgrading with dpkg -i, the meson install-log
    manifest, and fcitx5-diagnose as the which-version-is-loaded check).
  * Versioning moves to date-based MM.DD.N (first release of a day is .0);
    this is the first under that scheme and supersedes 0.3.1.

 -- RevolutionLA <revolutionla@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 08:50:00 +0800

fcitx5-nextless (0.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bug-fix release, no new configuration surface:
      - the capture sweep no longer deletes another session's in-flight WAV in
        the shared $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nextless directory (ownership by pid).
      - the local punctuator gives up after three consecutive failures instead
        of costing every utterance the full timeout.
      - nextless-get-models verifies every archive against a pinned sha256
        before extracting, and requires the punctuation binary when
        --punctuation is asked.
      - install-deb.sh refuses to install an unverifiable .deb.

 -- RevolutionLA <revolutionla@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 20:20:00 +0800

